{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetHTwPBNDmwFZmXtgsm5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me document my analysis findings before proceeding to design.\n\n## Summary of Repository Findings\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions shipments from CREATED to CONFIRMED status, supports idempotent retries, rejects CANCELLED shipments with HTTP 409, and rejects unknown shipments with HTTP 404.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-14`\n- ShipmentStatus enum: `Shipment.kt:23-27` with three states: CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- ShipmentController: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56` currently has create, getById, list\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` with save, findById, existsById, findAll methods\n- Exception handling: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt` defines ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- ErrorCode enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37` - currently no conflict-related codes for shipments\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28` centralizes error handling\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- No service layer; controllers work directly with repositories\n- Error handling via exceptions, not response objects\n- All endpoints return response bodies, not just status codes\n- Tests assert on both status codes and JSON response bodies\n- Tests check `error.code` in the error envelope for failures\n- In-memory repository pattern for no external dependencies\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — must add error code for state conflicts\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add the confirm endpoint method\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for all confirm scenarios\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotency: confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment must succeed and return the same shipment without error\n- State validation: must allow CREATED→CONFIRMED but reject CANCELLED transitions\n- Not following the error envelope pattern\n- Tests that don't verify state persisted (per testing-and-verification skill)\n\n**Open questions:** None. The ticket is complete and unambiguous.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` error code to the ErrorCode enum. This code will be used when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Takes the shipmentId as a path variable\n   - Retrieves the shipment from repository\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - If status is CREATED or CONFIRMED, saves the shipment with CONFIRMED status\n   - Returns the updated shipment with 200 OK status\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test cases:\n   - Confirms a CREATED shipment → transitions to CONFIRMED, verified via separate GET\n   - Confirms an already-CONFIRMED shipment → succeeds, returns same shipment, verified via separate GET\n   - Confirms a CANCELLED shipment → returns 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code, verified that shipment unchanged via GET\n   - Confirms a non-existent shipment → returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n**Alternatives considered and rejected:**\n\n1. **Alternative**: Add a separate `ShipmentService` layer between controller and repository\n   - Rejected: The existing codebase has no service layer (OrderController also works directly with repository), so this would violate the architecture convention and add unnecessary complexity.\n\n2. **Alternative**: Use `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` for the conflict when confirming a cancelled shipment\n   - Rejected: This error code is semantically incorrect (the shipment exists, but its state is invalid). A new code makes the intent clear to clients.\n\n3. **Alternative**: Allow transitions from any state to CONFIRMED\n   - Rejected: The ticket explicitly rejects CANCELLED→CONFIRMED with a 409, indicating state validation is required.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nFor confirming a CREATED shipment (happy path):\n1. POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n2. Controller retrieves shipment from repository\n3. Shipment status is CREATED\n4. Controller creates new Shipment object with status=CONFIRMED\n5. Controller calls repository.save()\n6. Repository stores updated shipment\n7. Controller returns Shipment with 200 OK status\n8. Caller issues GET /shipments/S-1 to verify persistence\n9. GET returns the CONFIRMED shipment\n\nFor confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment (idempotent retry):\n1. POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (second time)\n2. Controller retrieves shipment from repository\n3. Shipment status is already CONFIRMED\n4. Controller creates new Shipment with status=CONFIRMED (same)\n5. Controller calls repository.save()\n6. Repository overwrites with identical data\n7. Controller returns Shipment with 200 OK status\n8. Status is identical to before\n\nFor confirming a CANCELLED shipment (error case):\n1. POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n2. Controller retrieves shipment from repository\n3. Shipment status is CANCELLED\n4. Controller throws ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n5. GlobalExceptionHandler catches exception\n6. Returns 409 response with error envelope containing code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n7. Caller issues GET /shipments/S-1 to verify no state change\n8. GET returns unchanged CANCELLED shipment\n\nFor confirming a non-existent shipment:\n1. POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm\n2. Controller retrieves shipment from repository\n3. repository.findById() returns null\n4. Controller throws ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)\n5. GlobalExceptionHandler catches exception\n6. Returns 404 response with error envelope containing code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: confirms a created shipment**\n   - Creates S-1 in CREATED status\n   - Calls POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n   - Asserts response body contains status=CONFIRMED\n   - Issues separate GET /shipments/S-1\n   - Asserts GET response also shows CONFIRMED status\n\n2. **Test: confirms an already-confirmed shipment**\n   - Creates S-1 in CREATED status\n   - First POST /shipments/S-1/confirm → CONFIRMED\n   - Second POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (retry)\n   - Asserts second response body contains status=CONFIRMED\n   - Issues separate GET /shipments/S-1\n   - Asserts GET response still shows CONFIRMED (no regression)\n\n3. **Test: rejects confirming a cancelled shipment**\n   - Creates S-1, then directly saves it with CANCELLED status (via repository)\n   - Calls POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n   - Asserts response status is 409 Conflict\n   - Asserts error.code = SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - Issues separate GET /shipments/S-1\n   - Asserts GET response status is 200 and shipment still CANCELLED\n\n4. **Test: rejects confirming a non-existent shipment**\n   - Calls POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm\n   - Asserts response status is 404 Not Found\n   - Asserts error.code = SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1389,"cache_read_input_tokens":18755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1389},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"363f4ca8-86b8-4877-b265-6ebd6e93b52f","uuid":"8d97b9d5-ee55-4fa5-9ae5-1e80845f27bc","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:47:38.324Z","request_id":"req_011CetHTvgkiXGzzRYPaXXCf"}
