e ticket requires rejecting CANCELLED→CONFIRMED transitions with HTTP 409. This needs a specific error code so clients can distinguish it from other conflicts. Necessary.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added `confirm()` method\n   - **Why it had to change**: The ticket explicitly asks for `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`. Necessary.\n   - **Method logic review**:\n     - Retrieves shipment, throws 404 if not found ✓\n     - Rejects CANCELLED status with 409 and SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE ✓\n     - Creates new Shipment with CONFIRMED status (idempotent: works for both CREATED→CONFIRMED and CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED) ✓\n     - Saves and returns the updated shipment ✓\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 4 new test methods\n   - **Why it had to change**: Tests are required per the ticket. Necessary.\n   - **Test coverage review**:\n     - Each test exercises the call and asserts on response body ✓\n     - Each state-changing call has a separate GET request asserting persistence ✓\n     - The refused calls (cancelled, not found) have separate GET requests verifying no state change ✓\n     - Error code assertions present in conflict and not-found tests ✓\n     - Follows testing-and-verification skill requirements ✓\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All ticket requirements are satisfied.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm to transition CREATED shipments to CONFIRMED status, with idempotent retries, rejecting CANCELLED shipments (409) and unknown shipments (404)\n\nChanged       ApiError.kt — added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code for state conflict scenarios\n              ShipmentController.kt — added confirm(shipmentId) endpoint method that validates status and transitions to CONFIRMED\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 4 test methods covering CREATED→CONFIRMED transition, idempotent retry, CANCELLED rejection, and 404 handling\n\nTests         confirms a created shipment — verifies transition with separate GET persistence check\n              confirms an already-confirmed shipment without error — verifies idempotent retry with separate GET check\n              rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with conflict error — verifies 409 with error code and separate GET unchanged check\n              rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with not found error — verifies 404 with error code\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test from sample-service/\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS with 17 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors (added 4 new tests to 13 existing)\n\nNot done      Nothing — all ticket requirements implemented, tested, and verified\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3334,"cache_read_input_tokens":25349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3334},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"363f4ca8-86b8-4877-b265-6ebd6e93b52f","uuid":"83cd38ed-137f-45d0-9539-08cc557dd4d8","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:48:21.882Z","request_id":"req_011CetHY3eKNBQYDoNV7Nh35"}
